UMASK(2)                       P32W Unix                        UMASK(2)

NAME
       umask - set the file creation mask

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/stat.h>

       int umask(int mask);

DESCRIPTION
       umask sets the file creation mask of the calling process to
       mask & 0777 and returns the old one. The permission bits set
       in the mask are cleared from the mode given to open(2),
       creat(2) and mkdir(2) when they create a file. The mask is
       inherited by fork(2) and kept across exec(2); a process
       started by the kernel has 022.

RETURN VALUE
       The previous mask. The call cannot fail.

SEE ALSO
       open(2), mkdir(2), chmod(2), sh(1)

BUGS
       mknod(2) ignores the mask. The prototype is in <sys/stat.h>,
       not <unistd.h>.
